[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   TEP-9 step 098 -- RTG nuclear-decay channel
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Each Voyager carries three MHW-RTG units powered by Pu-238 alpha
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   decay (half-life 87.7 yr).  The electrical power record is therefore
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   a continuous ~44-year monitor of a *nuclear* clock -- a process class
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   distinct from both the electronic quartz oscillator (SCLK channel)
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   and the macroscopic orbital dynamics (comet channel).  This is the
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   "nuclear processes in the power engine" channel requested for the
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   TEP-9 analysis.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Data
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   The channel uses the published historical RTG performance dataset
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   (Whiting & Woerner 2023, doi:10.5061/dryad.1zcrjdfw2), which collates
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   the JPL MHW-RTG telemetry record: normalized electrical power versus
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   time for the Voyager 1 and Voyager 2 total missions and for each
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   individual RTG unit, through August 2021.  This is real telemetry --
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   129 Voyager-1 and 89 Voyager-2 total-mission epochs plus five
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   per-unit series -- not literature anchors.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Pedigree facts encoded from the dataset README (used in the
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   analysis):
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   * values are normalized to the beginning-of-mission power (highest
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   point within 30 days of BOM); absolute watts use the tabulated
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   PBOM (V1 total 471 We, V2 total 476 We);
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   * the first ~13.3 years are spacecraft-reported power;
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   * post-13.3-year points are recorded at epochs where an RTG current
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   dropped one telemetry bit (0.039 A for VG1, 0.038 A for VG2), so
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   the late series is bit-quantized at the ~1 % level;
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   * Voyager 2 RTG #3 telemetry was lost ~700 h after launch; the V2
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   total is reconstructed from units 1-2 plus a fixed bus-voltage
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   correction;
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   * literature power anchors (literature_anchors.json) are retained as
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   an independent cross-check on the fitted model.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Physics of the channel
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Alpha-decay rates are exponentially sensitive to the effective fine
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   structure constant through the Gamow penetrability exponent
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   G = pi Z1 Z2 alpha / beta ,   beta = v_rel/c ,
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   lambda ~ exp(-2 G)  =>  delta lambda / lambda ~ -2 G delta alpha_eff / alpha_eff .
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   For Pu-238 -> U-234 + alpha (Q = 5.59 MeV, Z1 Z2 = 184) the exponent
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   evaluates to G ~ 76, so the decay rate amplifies any constants
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   shift by ~150x: a delta alpha_eff / alpha_eff step at a
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   lapse-boundary crossing of comet-channel strength (~1e-2) would
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   appear as an order-unity step in thermal power -- far above the
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   bit-quantization floor.  The bound is
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   process-specific by construction: the TEP framework treats
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   electronic, nuclear and gravitational/dynamical couplings to A(phi)
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   as potentially different, so the RTG bound constrains the *nuclear*
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   channel without assuming it equals the orbital channel.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   Signatures tested
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   1. Level step at each crossing epoch: ln P = a + b t + s H(t-t_cx);
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   a constants step changes the instantaneous decay-rate power
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   (level), so s is the channel-relevant statistic.  t-test on s.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   2. Slope change at each crossing epoch: a post-crossing change in
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   the effective decay constant shows as a break in b.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   3. Per-RTU consistency: the same tests on the five functioning
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   per-unit series (3 x VG1, 2 x VG2).
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   4. VG1 - VG2 differential normalized power: removes the common-mode
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   degradation model and exposes craft-specific residuals around
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   each craft's own crossings.
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   5. Cross-check: the fitted model evaluated at the published
[2026-09-20 12:18:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 098]   literature-anchor epochs.
